# Deny everything, then name what the Dockerfile copies.
#
# A deny-list was one ignored directory behind reality: `target`, `web/node_modules`
# and `.git` were listed, and everything since — `.claude/worktrees` with a checkout
# per agent, each with its own target/ and node_modules/ — was not. That is 56 GB of
# build context tarred and handed to the daemon to build a 600-file binary, and the
# next big directory anyone adds would have joined it silently.
*

!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!.sqlx
!crates
!api
!web

# Re-excluded inside what was allowed back in: the dashboard's dependencies are
# installed in the image, and its build output is produced there.
web/node_modules
web/dist
